<body>
    <h1>How to Deploy IGEL OS 12 with IGEL OS Creator (OSC)</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>With the IGEL OS Creator (OSC), you can install IGEL OS 12 on an=
y supporting device. Moreover, you can use the IGEL OS Creator to recover a=
 broken installation of IGEL OS that cannot boot anymore.&nbsp;</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-war=
ning">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-error confluence-inform=
ation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>Installing the IGEL OS operating system via OSC destroys all data on the=
 target device=E2=80=99s mass storage device (hard disk, flash memory, SSD)=
.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-DevicesSupportedbyIGELO=
S12"><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-default">Devices Supported by IGEL OS=
 12</span></h2>
<p>For a detailed list, see&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net=
/wiki/spaces/ENLITEHARDWAREP/pages/74908060" data-linked-resource-id=3D"749=
08060" data-linked-resource-version=3D"46" data-linked-resource-type=3D"pag=
e">/wiki/spaces/ENLITEHARDWAREP/pages/74908060</a>.</p>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-Licensing">Licensing</h=
2>
<p><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-blue3">For information on licensing, se=
e&nbsp;</span><a class=3D"unresolved" href=3D"#">Essential IGEL Licensing F=
AQ</a> .</p>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-CreateUSBInstallationMe=
dium">Create USB Installation Medium</h2>
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-Windows">Windows</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Download the ZIP archive for OS Creator from the <a class=3D"external-li=
nk" href=3D"https://www.igel.com/software-downloads/igel-os-12-secure-endpo=
int/" rel=3D"nofollow">IGEL Download Server</a>. <br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Unzip the contents into a local directory.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Connect a USB memory stick with at least 4 GB capacity to the computer.<=
br>
All existing data on the USB memory stick will be destroyed.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Double-click the&nbsp;<code>preparestick.exe</code> &nbsp; &nbsp;file fr=
om the unzipped directory.<br>
If you are in the "administrators" group, the program will start after you =
have confirmed a dialog. If you are not in the "administrators" group, you =
must enter the administrator password to start the program.<br>
The dropdown menu&nbsp;<strong>Isofile</strong>&nbsp;shows the ISO file con=
tained in the unzipped directory, e.g.&nbsp;<code>osc12.01.110.iso</code>.<=
/p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper con=
fluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image=
-center" alt=3D"image-20240927-081936.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" s=
rc=3D"4e8d33be500d2d39f1a3dddab23d569430ac85abb8344e9011fb31bf67498656" dat=
a-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73=
302531/image-20240927-081936.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1727425=
177397&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"325" data-width=3D=
"407" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"179077=
859" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attach=
ment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-20240927-081936.png" data=
-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-con=
tent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302531" data=
-linked-resource-container-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"6830a229-f3f7-49=
63-9351-879f83b591ff" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"373"></span>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Under&nbsp;<strong>Destination USB stick</strong>, select the USB storag=
e medium on which you would like to save the installation data.<br>
It is recommended that you only have one USB storage medium connected durin=
g this procedure. If you accidentally select the wrong medium, all data on =
it will be lost.<br>
Generally speaking, the list of available USB storage media is refreshed au=
tomatically. If, however, you would like to refresh it manually, click on <=
strong>View &gt; Refresh USB Device List</strong>.</p><span class=3D"conflu=
ence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-=
size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"image-20=
240927-082055.png" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"53c3a613252329d3e8=
3fea1ee890bcacdf7b994f2c5409c7092d0e32600242e4" data-image-src=3D"https://i=
gel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302531/image-20240927-08=
2055.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1727425256995&amp;cacheVersion=
=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"325" data-width=3D"407" data-unresolved-c=
omment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"178716757" data-linked-resour=
ce-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resou=
rce-default-alias=3D"image-20240927-082055.png" data-base-url=3D"https://ig=
el-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png"=
 data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302531" data-linked-resource-contai=
ner-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"7ef49333-b758-4aeb-971c-527f3b58f219" d=
ata-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"373"></span>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Click&nbsp;<strong>Start writing process</strong>.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Confirm the following dialog:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file=
-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"=
confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image-border image-left" width=
=3D"400" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"356ea7a30d3c5abf81f1fcffc5d4b602b43e280a10=
e490deeab955a8568124b8" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/w=
iki/download/attachments/73302531/OSC_AllDataWill%20BeOverwritten2.jpg?vers=
ion=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364686516&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=
=3Dv2" data-height=3D"147" data-width=3D"404" data-unresolved-comment-count=
=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73309100" data-linked-resource-version=3D=
"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-a=
lias=3D"OSC_AllDataWill BeOverwritten2.jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-j=
ira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg" da=
ta-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302531" data-linked-resource-container=
-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"98296e1b-aa1d-4d65-a849-7e79bd081d9d" data=
-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"145"></span>
<p><br>
In the program window, the progress of the process is shown.</p><span class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded=
-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-im=
age-border image-left" width=3D"400" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"06762c7be180f9=
d278e6160bde27d1e4449b0fbfd72743e3e6825dccc872c8a2" data-image-src=3D"https=
://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302531/image-2022-11=
-25_12-16-47.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364686510&amp;cache=
Version=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"485" data-width=3D"655" data-unres=
olved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73309301" data-linked-=
resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked=
-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2022-11-25_12-16-47.png" data-base-url=3D"=
https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"=
image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302531" data-linked-resou=
rce-container-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"5736a9e6-b010-4919-9b57-2c22e=
076ecc0" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"295"></span>
<p><br>
When the process is finished, a message window is displayed.</p><span class=
=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded=
-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-im=
age-border image-left" width=3D"300" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"dac8b8db7347c2=
d9bc83208424b4af17c2dfe8fb2b7300e272415a11917ee2ab" data-image-src=3D"https=
://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302531/OSC_ProcessCo=
mplete4.jpg?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364686504&amp;cacheVersi=
on=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"147" data-width=3D"253" data-unresolved=
-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73309123" data-linked-resou=
rce-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-reso=
urce-default-alias=3D"OSC_ProcessComplete4.jpg" data-base-url=3D"https://ig=
el-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg=
" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302531" data-linked-resource-conta=
iner-version=3D"21" data-media-id=3D"4469e5a2-7e5f-4712-ab4f-22c82fc370c0" =
data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"174"></span>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Close the message window and the program.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>After about 3 seconds, remove the USB memory stick.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If you remove the USB memory stick too early, the writing process may st=
ill need to be completed. In this case, the data on the memory stick gets c=
orrupted.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>The USB memory stick for OSC installation is ready for use.</p>
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-Linux">Linux</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Download the ZIP archive for OS Creator from <a class=3D"external-link" =
data-card-appearance=3D"inline" href=3D"https://www.igel.com/software-downl=
oads/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.igel.com/software-downloads/</a>.</p>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Unzip the contents into a local directory.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>You will need the ISO file (e.g., osc12.4.1.iso) from this directory to =
create a bootable medium.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Connect a USB memory stick with&nbsp;at least 4 GB&nbsp;capacity to the =
computer.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>All existing data on the USB memory stick will be destroyed.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"5">
<li>
<p>Open a terminal emulator and enter the command&nbsp;<code>dmesg</code>&n=
bsp;to determine the device name of the USB memory stick.<br>
Example output:&nbsp;<br><code>[...]</code> <br><code>[19514.742229] scsi 3=
:0:0:0: Direct-Access JetFlash Transcend 8GB 1100 PQ: 0 ANSI: 6</code> <br>=
<code>[19514.742805] sd 3:0:0:0: Attached scsi generic sg1 type 0</code> <b=
r><code>[19514.744688] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb] 15425536 512-byte logical blocks: =
(7.89 GB/7.35 GiB)</code> <br><code>[19514.745370] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb] Write =
Protect is off</code> <br><code>[19514.745376] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb] Mode Sense=
: 43 (0) 00 00 00</code> <br><code>[19514.746040] sd 3:0:0:0: [sdb] Write c=
ache: enabled, read cache: enabled, doesn't support DPO or FUA</code> <br><=
code>[19514.752438] sdb: sdb1</code><br><br>
In this example, the device name searched for is&nbsp;<code>/dev/sdb</code>=
.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>Ensure that you have determined the correct device name. If you use the =
wrong device name, the <code>dd</code> command in the next step can destroy=
 your operating system.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<ol start=3D"6">
<li>
<p>The following command writes the installation data to the USB memory sti=
ck (example):<br><code>dd if=3Dosc12.4.1.iso of=3D/dev/sdX bs=3D1M oflag=3D=
direct</code> <br>
Replace&nbsp;<code>sdX&nbsp;</code>with the device name of the USB memory s=
tick that you have determined.&nbsp;<br>
When the <code>dd</code>&nbsp;command has terminated, you can see the termi=
nal emulator input prompt again.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Wait for about 3 seconds after the&nbsp;<code>dd</code>&nbsp;command has=
 terminated, and remove the USB memory stick.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If you remove the USB memory stick too early, the writing process may st=
ill need to be completed. In this case, the data on the memory stick gets c=
orrupted.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>The USB memory stick for OSC installation is ready for use.</p>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-CreateDVDInstallationMe=
dium">Create DVD Installation Medium&nbsp;</h2>
<p>The ISO file in the installation directory for OSC is a so-called hybrid=
 image. It can not only be copied onto USB storage devices but can also be =
used to create a bootable DVD.</p>
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-BurnISOImage(Windows)">=
Burn ISO Image (Windows)</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>In Explorer, open the directory that contains the ISO file.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Right-click on the&nbsp;ISO file.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Select&nbsp;<strong>Burn disc image</strong>.</p></li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-BurnISOImage(Linux)">Bu=
rn ISO Image (Linux)</h3>
<p>Under Linux, various burning programs with a graphical user interface or=
 for the command line are available.</p>
<p>The&nbsp;<a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://help.ubuntu.com/comm=
unity/BurningIsoHowto#Burning_from_Ubuntu" rel=3D"nofollow">Ubuntu Wiki</a>=
&nbsp;explains how to burn an ISO image onto a DVD using several programs.<=
/p>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withIGELOSCreator(OSC)-BootSettings">Boot Sett=
ings</h2>
<p>OSC works on systems with BIOS and UEFI.</p>
<p>Your system must support booting from USB storage media or from a DVD. T=
his may already be enabled, or you may have to enable it yourself.</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>IGEL OS 12 supports UEFI Secure Boot. Refer to the manual of your device=
's manufacturer to learn whether your device supports Secure Boot and how t=
o enable it. Enabling Secure Boot often consists of two steps. First, the b=
oot mode has to be changed to UEFI Boot in the BIOS; after that, Secure Boo=
t can be activated, also in the BIOS. For instructions on how to check whet=
her Secure Boot has been properly enabled, see<a class=3D"unresolved" href=
=3D"#">Verifying that Secure Boot is Enabled</a> .</p>
<p>For UEFI Secure Boot on devices manufactured by IGEL, see <a class=3D"un=
resolved" href=3D"#">UEFI Secure Boot Enabling Guides</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If IGEL OS fails to boot in UEFI mode, try switching to <strong>Force Le=
gacy (non UEFI) boot</strong>. IGEL OS will then be installed in legacy/BIO=
S mode.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wra=
pper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-ima=
